// =====================================================================
// FRP tools benchmark — executable, deterministic, document-generating
// (`npm run benchmark:frp`)
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------
// Scores 8 FRP tools (7 competitors + this repo's Adaptive Engine)
// against a 12-device corpus spanning Android 12 → 16, 8 brands, 5
// chipset families. Two output artifacts, both generated BY THIS TEST:
//   docs/benchmarks/frp-tools-benchmark-2026.json  (machine-readable)
//   docs/FRP-TOOLS-BENCHMARK-2026.md               (the full report)
//
// METHOD LAW (repo rule, non-negotiable):
//   * OUR tool is scored by RUNNING the real engine
//     (computeBand / buildAdaptivePlan / evaluateParallelLanes / LAB_LEDGER).
//   * COMPETITORS are scored by a DOCUMENTED-CAPABILITY MODEL — fixed
//     deterministic tables distilled from public evidence
//     (FRP-ALGORITHM-ANALYSIS.md, RESEARCH-2026-FRP.md,
//     docs/COMPARISON-2026-FINAL.md, the A15/16 patch dossier). Their
//     binaries are not executed here; the doc says so on every page.
//   * No RNG: same inputs → byte-identical outputs. An input hash is
//     printed for reproducibility.
//   * Honesty self-audit: the generated document is scanned for banned
//     marketing phrases before it is written; violations fail the run.
// =====================================================================

